---
/**
 * BileAcidLoop — "the pool that is used five times a day". A bile acid balance
 * calculator for the lesson's worked problem. Three sliders (pool size, cycles per day,
 * fractional reabsorption per cycle) and a toggle (ileal uptake intact or blocked) feed the
 * lesson's rules: delivery = pool x cycles; fecal loss = delivery x (1 - f); at steady state
 * synthesis = fecal loss; pool renewed per day = fecal loss / pool x 100. A log-scale gauge
 * sets the loss against the lesson's human review range of 0.20 to 0.40 g a day and against
 * the textbook 95 percent figure, which does not close with it. Arithmetic on assumed inputs,
 * not a measurement. The component keeps its historical file name; it holds no rehydration
 * content. Self-contained vanilla-TS Astro island. Original.
 */
---

<figure class="ora card" data-ora>
  <figcaption class="ora-head"><span>Bile acid balance — a pool used about five times a day</span><span class="ora-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <svg class="ora-svg" viewBox="0 0 340 140" role="img" aria-label="A schematic loop of two labelled blocks, the liver and the gut lumen. An arrow from the liver to the gut carries the delivery to the ileum, an arrow back to the liver carries what is recovered at the ileum, a short arrow out of the gut carries the loss in stool, and a short arrow into the liver carries synthesis from cholesterol" data-loop></svg>

  <div class="ora-controls">
    <label class="ora-slabel"><span>Pool size <em data-out="pool">3.5</em> g</span>
      <input type="range" data-in="pool" min="20" max="50" step="1" value="35" />
    </label>
    <label class="ora-slabel"><span>Cycles per day <em data-out="cyc">5</em></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="cyc" min="3" max="8" step="1" value="5" />
    </label>
    <label class="ora-slabel"><span>Fractional reabsorption per cycle <em data-out="f">98.3</em> percent <small data-capnote></small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="f" min="850" max="995" step="1" value="983" />
    </label>
    <fieldset class="ora-radios" data-radios>
      <legend>Ileal bile acid uptake</legend>
      <label class="ora-radio"><input type="radio" value="intact" checked /> <span>ileal uptake intact</span></label>
      <label class="ora-radio"><input type="radio" value="blocked" /> <span>ileal uptake blocked</span></label>
    </fieldset>
  </div>

  <svg class="ora-svg" viewBox="0 0 340 132" role="img" aria-label="A logarithmic gauge of fecal bile acid loss in grams per day, from 0.01 to 10, with a shaded band for the human review range of 0.20 to 0.40 grams per day, a bar for the loss at the current settings and a marker for the loss at 95 percent reabsorption" data-gauge></svg>

  <dl class="ora-readout">
    <div><dt>Delivery to the ileum = pool × cycles</dt><dd data-r="d"></dd><small data-r="dsub"></small></div>
    <div><dt>Fecal loss = delivery × (1 − f)</dt><dd data-r="loss"></dd><small data-r="lsub"></small></div>
    <div><dt>Required synthesis, as a share of the pool per day</dt><dd data-r="syn"></dd><small data-r="ssub"></small></div>
    <div><dt>Reabsorption per cycle used by the sketch</dt><dd data-r="fuse"></dd><small data-r="fsub"></small></div>
  </dl>

  <div class="ora-math" data-math></div>
  <div class="ora-why" data-why role="status">
    <p data-why-main></p>
    <p data-why-note></p>
  </div>
  <p class="ora-assume">In this sketch: steady state, and the whole pool recirculates each cycle, which is the lesson’s own assumption. Pool size, cycles per day and reabsorption per cycle are set independently, so some combinations may not occur in a person. The reference values are the lesson’s human review figures: pool 3.5 g, about 5 cycles a day, about 95 percent reabsorbed per cycle, fecal loss 200 to 400 mg a day. Made up for the sketch: the slider limits (pool 2.0 to 5.0 g, 3 to 8 cycles a day, 85.0 to 99.5 percent), the 90.0 percent cap used when ileal uptake is blocked (the lesson’s sensitivity case uses 90 percent; the ASBT-deleted mice excreted 10- to 20-fold more bile acid in stool, which this sketch does not reproduce), the logarithmic loss scale and the arrow thickness. Values are rounded for display: at the default the loss is 0.2975 g per day, so synthesis reads 8.5 percent of the pool, where the lesson, rounding the loss to 0.30 g first, gets 8.6 percent.</p>
  <p class="ora-foot">Rule to keep: at steady state synthesis equals fecal loss, and fecal loss is the delivered flux times the fraction that escapes reabsorption, so a small change in a number close to one moves the loss several-fold. The three textbook figures (a 3.5 g pool, about 5 cycles a day, about 95 percent reabsorbed) are rounded and do not close with a measured loss of 200 to 400 mg a day; that mismatch is the point, and the readouts are arithmetic on assumed inputs, not a measurement.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const ACCENT = '#0e7c86', ORANGE = '#c25f00', INK = '#4b4b55', FAINT = '#b9b9c2', BAND = '#f7dcc0';
  const CAP10 = 900; // reabsorption cap when ileal uptake is blocked, in tenths of a percent (made up for the sketch)
  const TEXTBOOK10 = 950; // the lesson's textbook 95 percent
  const BAND_LO = 0.2, BAND_HI = 0.4; // g per day, the lesson's human review range

  function el(name: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>): SVGElement {
    const e = document.createElementNS(NS, name);
    for (const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, String(attrs[k]));
    return e;
  }
  function need<T extends Element>(root: ParentNode, sel: string): T {
    const e = root.querySelector<T>(sel);
    if (!e) throw new Error('BileAcidLoop: missing ' + sel);
    return e;
  }
  function txt(parent: SVGElement, x: number, y: number, s: string, extra: Record<string, string | number> = {}): SVGElement {
    const t = el('text', { x, y, 'font-size': 9, fill: INK, ...extra });
    t.textContent = s;
    parent.appendChild(t);
    return t;
  }
  // arrow along one axis, with a triangular head at (x2, y2)
  function arrow(parent: SVGElement, x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number, w: number, color: string) {
    const head = 7, hw = 5 + w / 2;
    const dx = Math.sign(x2 - x1), dy = Math.sign(y2 - y1);
    parent.appendChild(el('line', { x1, y1, x2: x2 - dx * head, y2: y2 - dy * head, stroke: color, 'stroke-width': w }));
    const bx = x2 - dx * head, by = y2 - dy * head;
    const pts = dx !== 0
      ? `${x2},${y2} ${bx},${by - hw} ${bx},${by + hw}`
      : `${x2},${y2} ${bx - hw},${by} ${bx + hw},${by}`;
    parent.appendChild(el('polygon', { points: pts, fill: color }));
  }
  // number to at most dp decimals, trailing zeros removed
  const trim = (n: number, dp: number) => String(Number(n.toFixed(dp)));
  const eq = (n: number, dp: number) => (Math.abs(n - Number(n.toFixed(dp))) < 1e-9 ? '=' : '≈');
  // round half up with a small epsilon, so 2.275 shows as 2.28 and not 2.27
  const f2 = (n: number) => (Math.round(n * 100 + 1e-7) / 100).toFixed(2);
  // up to dp decimals, trailing zeros removed but never fewer than two decimals
  const dec = (n: number, dp: number) => {
    let t = n.toFixed(dp);
    while (t.length > 0 && t.endsWith('0') && t.length - t.indexOf('.') - 1 > 2) t = t.slice(0, -1);
    return t;
  };

  let uid = 0;
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ora]').forEach((root) => {
    uid += 1;
    const loop = need<SVGSVGElement>(root, '[data-loop]');
    const gauge = need<SVGSVGElement>(root, '[data-gauge]');
    const poolIn = need<HTMLInputElement>(root, '[data-in="pool"]');
    const cycIn = need<HTMLInputElement>(root, '[data-in="cyc"]');
    const fIn = need<HTMLInputElement>(root, '[data-in="f"]');
    const poolOut = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-out="pool"]');
    const cycOut = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-out="cyc"]');
    const fOut = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-out="f"]');
    const capNote = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-capnote]');
    const radioBox = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-radios]');
    const radios = Array.from(radioBox.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[type="radio"]'));
    radios.forEach((r) => { r.name = 'ora-uptake-' + uid; });
    const rD = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'dd[data-r="d"]');
    const rDs = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'small[data-r="dsub"]');
    const rL = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'dd[data-r="loss"]');
    const rLs = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'small[data-r="lsub"]');
    const rS = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'dd[data-r="syn"]');
    const rSs = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'small[data-r="ssub"]');
    const rF = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'dd[data-r="fuse"]');
    const rFs = need<HTMLElement>(root, 'small[data-r="fsub"]');
    const math = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-math]');
    const whyMain = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-why-main]');
    const whyNote = need<HTMLElement>(root, '[data-why-note]');

    // log gauge geometry: 0.01 to 10 g per day
    const GX0 = 20, GX1 = 320, LMIN = -2, LMAX = 1;
    const gx = (v: number) => GX0 + ((Math.log10(Math.min(Math.max(v, 0.01), 10)) - LMIN) / (LMAX - LMIN)) * (GX1 - GX0);

    function blocked(): boolean {
      return radios.some((r) => r.checked && r.value === 'blocked');
    }

    function render() {
      const pool10 = parseInt(poolIn.value, 10); // tenths of a gram
      const cyc = parseInt(cycIn.value, 10);
      const fSlider10 = parseInt(fIn.value, 10); // tenths of a percent
      const isBlocked = blocked();
      const capBinds = isBlocked && fSlider10 > CAP10;
      const f10 = isBlocked ? Math.min(fSlider10, CAP10) : fSlider10;

      const pool = pool10 / 10;
      const D = (pool10 * cyc) / 10; // g per day delivered to the ileum
      const escape = (1000 - f10) / 1000;
      const L = (pool10 * cyc * (1000 - f10)) / 10000; // g per day, fecal loss = synthesis
      const S = (L / pool) * 100; // percent of pool per day
      const recovered = D - L;
      const L95 = (pool10 * cyc * (1000 - TEXTBOOK10)) / 10000;
      const Lintact = (pool10 * cyc * (1000 - fSlider10)) / 10000;
      const L2 = Math.round(L * 100 + 1e-7) / 100; // as displayed, used for the band test
      const band = L2 < BAND_LO ? 'below' : L2 > BAND_HI ? 'above' : 'inside';
      const fShown = (n10: number) => (n10 / 10).toFixed(1);

      poolOut.textContent = pool.toFixed(1);
      cycOut.textContent = String(cyc);
      fOut.textContent = fShown(fSlider10);
      capNote.textContent = capBinds ? '(the toggle caps it at ' + fShown(CAP10) + ' percent)' : isBlocked ? '(at or below the toggle’s cap, so unchanged)' : '';

      // readouts
      rD.textContent = f2(D) + ' g per day';
      rDs.textContent = pool.toFixed(1) + ' g × ' + cyc + ' cycles per day';
      rL.textContent = f2(L) + ' g per day';
      rLs.textContent = (band === 'inside' ? 'inside' : band === 'above' ? 'above' : 'below') + ' the human review range, 0.20 to 0.40 g per day (loss as displayed)' + (isBlocked ? ' (drawn for comparison only)' : '');
      rS.textContent = S.toFixed(1) + ' percent of the pool';
      rSs.textContent = f2(L) + ' g per day, equal to the fecal loss at steady state';
      rF.textContent = fShown(f10) + ' percent';
      rFs.textContent = isBlocked ? (capBinds ? 'capped by the toggle (your slider: ' + fShown(fSlider10) + ')' : 'your slider value, already at or below the cap') : 'your slider value';

      // arithmetic, with units
      math.replaceChildren();
      const lossStr = dec(L, 4);
      const lines = [
        'delivery = pool × cycles = ' + pool.toFixed(1) + ' × ' + cyc + ' = ' + f2(D) + ' g per day',
        'fecal loss = delivery × (1 − f) = ' + f2(D) + ' × (1 − ' + trim(f10 / 1000, 3) + ') = ' + f2(D) + ' × ' + dec(escape, 3) + ' ' + eq(L, 4) + ' ' + lossStr + ' g per day ' + (eq(L, 2) === '=' ? '' : '≈ ' + f2(L) + ' g per day'),
        'synthesis = fecal loss, at steady state = ' + lossStr + ' g per day',
        'pool renewed per day = ' + lossStr + ' ÷ ' + pool.toFixed(1) + ' × 100 ' + eq(S, 1) + ' ' + S.toFixed(1) + ' percent' + (pool10 === 35 && cyc === 5 && f10 === 983 ? ' (the lesson, rounding the loss to 0.30 g first, gets 8.6)' : ''),
      ];
      for (const l of lines) {
        const d = document.createElement('div');
        d.textContent = l.trim();
        math.appendChild(d);
      }

      // loop schematic
      loop.replaceChildren();
      const wOf = (v: number) => 1.5 + 5.5 * Math.min(v / 40, 1);
      loop.appendChild(el('rect', { x: 14, y: 44, width: 90, height: 40, rx: 4, fill: '#fff', stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1.2 }));
      txt(loop, 59, 62, 'Liver', { 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-weight': 700 });
      txt(loop, 59, 75, 'bile acid pool ' + pool.toFixed(1) + ' g', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      loop.appendChild(el('rect', { x: 216, y: 44, width: 110, height: 40, rx: 4, fill: '#fff', stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1.2 }));
      txt(loop, 271, 62, 'Gut lumen', { 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-weight': 700 });
      txt(loop, 271, 75, 'duodenum to ileum', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      // delivery (liver to gut)
      arrow(loop, 104, 58, 216, 58, wOf(D), ACCENT);
      txt(loop, 160, 40, 'delivery to ileum', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      txt(loop, 160, 51, f2(D) + ' g per day', { 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-weight': 700 });
      // recovered (gut to liver)
      arrow(loop, 216, 72, 104, 72, wOf(recovered), ACCENT);
      txt(loop, 160, 87, isBlocked ? 'recovered (capped)' : 'recovered at ileum', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      txt(loop, 160, 98, isBlocked ? '(ASBT blocked)' : '(ASBT)', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      txt(loop, 160, 109, f2(recovered) + ' g per day', { 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-weight': 700 });
      // stool loss (out of gut)
      arrow(loop, 271, 84, 271, 108, wOf(L), ORANGE);
      txt(loop, 271, 119, 'lost in stool', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      txt(loop, 271, 130, f2(L) + ' g per day', { 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-weight': 700, fill: ORANGE });
      // synthesis (into liver)
      arrow(loop, 59, 108, 59, 84, wOf(L), INK);
      txt(loop, 59, 119, 'made from cholesterol', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      txt(loop, 59, 130, f2(L) + ' g per day', { 'text-anchor': 'middle', 'font-weight': 700 });

      // gauge
      gauge.replaceChildren();
      const bx0 = gx(BAND_LO), bx1 = gx(BAND_HI);
      gauge.appendChild(el('rect', { x: bx0, y: 22, width: bx1 - bx0, height: 40, fill: BAND }));
      txt(gauge, (bx0 + bx1) / 2, 15, 'human review range, 0.20 to 0.40 g per day', { 'text-anchor': 'middle' });
      const xL = gx(L);
      gauge.appendChild(el('rect', { x: GX0, y: 34, width: Math.max(xL - GX0, 1), height: 16, fill: isBlocked ? ORANGE : ACCENT }));
      const xv = xL < GX0 + 40 ? 'start' : xL > GX1 - 40 ? 'end' : 'middle';
      txt(gauge, xL, 31, f2(L), { 'text-anchor': xv, 'font-weight': 700 });
      // textbook 95 percent marker
      const x95 = gx(L95);
      gauge.appendChild(el('polygon', { points: `${x95},50 ${x95 + 5},56 ${x95},62 ${x95 - 5},56`, fill: '#fff', stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1.4 }));
      // axis
      const AY = 72;
      gauge.appendChild(el('line', { x1: GX0, y1: AY, x2: GX1, y2: AY, stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
      for (const d of [0.01, 0.1, 1, 10]) {
        const x = gx(d);
        gauge.appendChild(el('line', { x1: x, y1: AY, x2: x, y2: AY + 4, stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
        txt(gauge, x, AY + 15, String(d), { 'text-anchor': d === 0.01 ? 'start' : d === 10 ? 'end' : 'middle' });
      }
      for (const base of [0.01, 0.1, 1]) {
        for (let m = 2; m <= 9; m++) {
          const x = gx(base * m);
          gauge.appendChild(el('line', { x1: x, y1: AY, x2: x, y2: AY + 2, stroke: FAINT, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
        }
      }
      txt(gauge, GX0, AY + 28, 'fecal bile acid loss, g per day (log scale, bar starts at 0.01)', { 'text-anchor': 'start' });
      // legend
      gauge.appendChild(el('rect', { x: GX0, y: 107, width: 12, height: 9, fill: isBlocked ? ORANGE : ACCENT }));
      txt(gauge, GX0 + 17, 115, (isBlocked ? 'lost-uptake case in this sketch: ' : 'your settings: ') + f2(L) + ' g per day', { 'text-anchor': 'start' });
      const lx = GX0 + 6;
      gauge.appendChild(el('polygon', { points: `${lx},119 ${lx + 5},124 ${lx},129 ${lx - 5},124`, fill: '#fff', stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1.4 }));
      txt(gauge, GX0 + 17, 127, '95 percent reabsorption, same pool and cycles: ' + dec(L95, 3) + ' g per day', { 'text-anchor': 'start' });

      // status
      const fPct = fShown(f10);
      let main: string;
      if (!isBlocked) {
        main = 'In this sketch, a pool of ' + pool.toFixed(1) + ' g used ' + cyc + ' times a day delivers ' + f2(D) + ' g per day to the ileum; with ' + fPct + ' percent reabsorbed per cycle, ' + f2(L) + ' g per day escapes reabsorption, and at steady state synthesis must replace it, which is ' + S.toFixed(1) + ' percent of the pool per day.';
      } else {
        main = 'In this sketch, with ileal uptake blocked, reabsorption is held at or below ' + fShown(CAP10) + ' percent per cycle' + (capBinds ? ' (your slider says ' + fShown(fSlider10) + ', so the cap applies)' : ' (your slider is already at ' + fPct + ', at or below the cap, so the cap changes nothing)') + ', so ' + f2(L) + ' g per day escapes from a delivery of ' + f2(D) + ' g per day, and at steady state synthesis must replace ' + S.toFixed(1) + ' percent of the pool per day.';
      }
      whyMain.textContent = main;

      const parts: string[] = [];
      if (isBlocked) {
        parts.push('This is not the mouse ASBT-knockout result: those mice, a different species with a pool that fell about 80 percent, excreted 10- to 20-fold more bile acid in stool, and the lesson says the same consequences are not shown in people. Here the lesson’s 90 percent sensitivity case is applied to the human review pool and cycles, and the pool stays at the size you set.');
        if (capBinds) parts.push('In this sketch the loss is ' + (Lintact > 0 ? (L / Lintact).toFixed(1) : '—') + ' times the loss with uptake intact at your slider setting.');
        parts.push('The human review range is drawn for comparison only.');
      } else {
        if (band === 'inside') {
          parts.push('In this sketch, that loss, as displayed, is inside the 0.20 to 0.40 g per day in the lesson’s human review figures.');
        } else {
          parts.push('In this sketch, that loss, as displayed, is ' + band + ' the 0.20 to 0.40 g per day in the lesson’s human review figures, so these settings fall outside the observed band.');
        }
        if (f10 === TEXTBOOK10) {
          parts.push('Your reabsorption is the textbook 95.0 percent.');
        } else {
          parts.push('In this sketch, 95 percent reabsorption with your pool and cycles would give ' + dec(L95, 3) + ' g per day, for comparison.');
        }
        if (pool10 === 35 && cyc === 5) {
          parts.push('With the lesson’s own 3.5 g pool and 5 cycles a day, 95 percent gives 0.875 g per day, two to four times the measured 200 to 400 mg a day, so the rounded textbook figures do not close.');
        }
      }
      whyNote.textContent = parts.join(' ');
    }

    [poolIn, cycIn, fIn].forEach((g) => g.addEventListener('input', render));
    radios.forEach((r) => r.addEventListener('change', render));
    render();
  });
</script>

<style is:global>
  .ora { padding: var(--ddp-space-3) var(--ddp-space-4) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-5) 0; }
  .ora-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .ora-chip { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .ora-svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto var(--ddp-space-2); height: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ora-controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 var(--ddp-space-2); }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .ora-controls { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .ora-slabel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.15rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .ora-slabel small { font-size: inherit; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .ora-slabel em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ddp-color-accent); font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); }
  .ora-slabel input[type="range"] { accent-color: var(--ddp-color-accent); }
  .ora-radios { margin: 0; padding: 0; border: 0; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .ora-radios legend { padding: 0; margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }
  .ora-radio { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .ora-radio input { accent-color: var(--ddp-color-accent); margin: 0; }
  .ora-readout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: var(--ddp-space-2); margin: var(--ddp-space-2) 0; padding: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-3); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ddp-color-accent) 8%, transparent); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ora-readout div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; }
  .ora-readout dt { font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .ora-readout dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); font-weight: 700; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .ora-readout small { font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.35; }
  .ora-math { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; margin: var(--ddp-space-2) 0; padding-left: 0.55rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--ddp-color-accent); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .ora-why { margin: 0 0 var(--ddp-space-2); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; min-height: 8em; }
  .ora-why p { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .ora-assume { margin: 0 0 var(--ddp-space-2); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  .ora-foot { margin: var(--ddp-space-2) 0 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); border-left: 3px solid var(--ddp-color-secondary); padding-left: 0.55rem; }
</style>
